cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PerturbNMF, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PerturbNMF: an end-to-end pipeline for consensus NMF on single-cell perturbation data"
abstract: >-
  PerturbNMF runs and evaluates consensus Non-negative Matrix Factorization
  (cNMF) on single-cell perturbation data such as CRISPR screens. It runs on a
  single workstation or laptop; optional SLURM runner scripts are included for
  users who want to distribute the work on a cluster.
  Stage 1 infers gene programs with
  sk-cNMF (CPU) or torch-cNMF (GPU). Stage 2 scores program quality with nine
  metrics and calibrates perturbation p-values via U-test, conditional
  randomization test, or matched-cell differential expression. Stage 3
  produces K-selection and QC plots, Excel summaries, and LLM-driven program
  annotation with PubTator3 literature mining.
